# The build context is the repository root, and almost none of it belongs in a
# build. Two entries here are load-bearing rather than cosmetic:
#
#   .env*   -- an image layer is permanent. A credential copied into layer three
#              survives every subsequent `rm` in layer four, and `docker history`
#              will hand it to anyone who pulls the image. Live mode's secrets
#              reach the container through a mount at runtime, never a COPY.
#   _opam/  -- a local opam switch built for arm64 Darwin. Copying it into a
#              Debian amd64 builder would be 1.5GB of transfer producing
#              binaries that cannot run.

.env
.env.*
*.env

_build/
_opam/
_coverage/
.venv/
.git/
.github/
.DS_Store
.superpowers/

docs/
bench/
test/
*.md
!README.md

Untitled
